# ralph egress policy -- deny by default.
#
# One extended regular expression per line, matched against the destination
# hostname. Anchor with ^...$ so that a rule for `github.com` cannot be matched
# by `github.com.attacker.example`.
#
# Edit with `ralph policy edit`, inspect with `ralph policy ls`.
# Keep this list as small as your work allows.

# --- Agent API and authentication (required) ---
# platform.claude.com handles OAuth token exchange, refresh and revocation for
# BOTH Console and claude.ai logins, and the first-run connectivity check pings
# it directly. Without it Claude Code fails to start with a 403 from this proxy.
^api\.anthropic\.com$
^platform\.claude\.com$
^claude\.ai$
^claude\.com$
^console\.anthropic\.com$
^statsig\.anthropic\.com$

# --- Optional Claude Code hosts (uncomment only if you need them) ---
# claude.ai MCP connectors, which are on by default for claude.ai logins.
# Leave blocked and set ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false to avoid the retries.
#^mcp-proxy\.anthropic\.com$
# Plugin downloads, native installer and auto-update checks.
#^downloads\.claude\.ai$
# Docs lookups by the built-in claude-code-guide agent.
#^code\.claude\.com$
# Operational telemetry and error reports. Blocked here by design; also set
# CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1 so nothing waits on them.
#^http-intake\.logs\.us5\.datadoghq\.com$
#^browser-intake-us5-datadoghq\.com$

# --- Package registries ---
^registry\.npmjs\.org$
^pypi\.org$
^files\.pythonhosted\.org$

# --- Source hosting ---
^github\.com$
^api\.github\.com$
^codeload\.github\.com$
^objects\.githubusercontent\.com$
^raw\.githubusercontent\.com$

# --- OS packages (needed to install things inside the sandbox) ---
^archive\.ubuntu\.com$
^security\.ubuntu\.com$
^ports\.ubuntu\.com$
^deb\.nodesource\.com$
